    <node id="Canada Pension Plan (CPP)">
      <data key="d0">Canada Pension Plan (CPP)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Pension Plan (CPP) is a social insurance program in Canada that provides retirement pensions and benefits to contributors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101146</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Quebec Pension Plan (QPP)">
      <data key="d0">Quebec Pension Plan (QPP)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Quebec Pension Plan (QPP) is a pension plan available to Quebec residents that offers retirement benefits, with slightly higher rates than CPP.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101146</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Employment Insurance (EI)">
      <data key="d0">Employment Insurance (EI)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Employment Insurance (EI) provides temporary financial assistance to unemployed individuals in Canada.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101147</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carbon-Fiber Spikes">
      <data key="d0">Carbon-Fiber Spikes</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced sprinting shoes designed to provide enhanced performance for sprinters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101147</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T4 Box References">
      <data key="d0">T4 Box References</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">T4 Box References include various boxes on the T4 slip that report employee contributions and earnings for tax purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101147</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="2025 Tax Year">
      <data key="d0">2025 Tax Year</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The 2025 Tax Year refers to the period for tax accounting in Canada, detailed in the CRA Payroll Deductions Tables.&lt;SEP&gt;The 2025 Tax Year outlines future tax rates and brackets that will be applicable for federal income taxation.&lt;SEP&gt;The 2025 Tax Year refers to the period in which capital gains taxation rules discussed in the content are applied.&lt;SEP&gt;The 2025 tax year is mentioned as the last updated period for the regulations concerning the First Home Savings Account (FHSA).&lt;SEP&gt;The 2025 Tax Year indicates the specific tax regulations and brackets that apply to income earned during that year in Alberta.&lt;SEP&gt;The 2025 Tax Year details the latest tax rates and brackets applicable to Quebec residents for that fiscal period.&lt;SEP&gt;The 2025 Tax Year is relevant for the most recent income tax rates and brackets effective in Saskatchewan as of that year.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca78b2360336d6f6222a6f4c95eb423&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b628c2e9232fe00bd1ee55c3ddc07d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6da06f6e3dca271d80baa141c0aef4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dd1ab2e92259b216c4f87314232a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-936dddac80917fe456d3727287e9f980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a71d4ab43b2c554a485b5c3822440d6b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772370274</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Max Insurable Earnings">
      <data key="d0">Max Insurable Earnings</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Max Insurable Earnings represent the highest amount on which employment insurance premiums are calculated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101147</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings (YMPE)">
      <data key="d0">Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings (YMPE)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings (YMPE) is the maximum amount of earnings on which Canada Pension Plan contributions are based.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101148</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contribution Rate">
      <data key="d0">Contribution Rate</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Contribution rate refers to the percentage of earnings that employees contribute to the Canada Pension Plan (CPP) and Employment Insurance (EI).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101148</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Basic Exemption">
      <data key="d0">Basic Exemption</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The basic exemption is the minimum amount of earnings that is excluded from calculation for CPP contributions, set at $3,500 per year.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101148</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maximum Employee Contribution">
      <data key="d0">Maximum Employee Contribution</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Maximum employee contribution represents the highest amount an employee can contribute to the Canada Pension Plan (CPP) or Employment Insurance (EI) in a given year.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101148</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Second Earnings Ceiling (YAMPE)">
      <data key="d0">Second Earnings Ceiling (YAMPE)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The second earnings ceiling, referred to as YAMPE, is the maximum threshold for contributions for enhanced CPP starting in 2024.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a149e8a923d92f6e23bd59e44524fceb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101149</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Box 14">
      <data key="d0">Box 14</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Box 14 refers to a specific box mentioned in a financial context that is capped at maximums.&lt;SEP&gt;Box 14 is used to report total employment income on T4 slips.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be3c8254ac3b81df856eab05e2babc4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041dc2e0b32226e0b7c758a7359523f3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101192</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Box 24">
      <data key="d0">Box 24</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Box 24 is referenced alongside Box 14 and is subject to caps in the financial context.&lt;SEP&gt;Box 24 is utilized for reporting EI contributions on T4 slips.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be3c8254ac3b81df856eab05e2babc4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041dc2e0b32226e0b7c758a7359523f3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101192</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Box 26">
      <data key="d0">Box 26</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Box 26 is mentioned in relation to financial caps and contributes to calculations involving CPP and EI.&lt;SEP&gt;Box 26 is used for reporting additional deductions or earnings on T4 slips.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be3c8254ac3b81df856eab05e2babc4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041dc2e0b32226e0b7c758a7359523f3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101192</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CPP">
      <data key="d0">CPP</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CPP refers to Canada Pension Plan contributions which generate non-refundable tax credits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be3c8254ac3b81df856eab05e2babc4e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101151</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="EI">
      <data key="d0">EI</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">EI refers to Employment Insurance premiums that also generate non-refundable tax credits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be3c8254ac3b81df856eab05e2babc4e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101151</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Federal Tax Rate">
      <data key="d0">Federal Tax Rate</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The federal tax rate is defined as 15%, applied to calculate non-refundable tax credits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be3c8254ac3b81df856eab05e2babc4e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101151</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CPP/EI Credit">
      <data key="d0">CPP/EI Credit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The CPP/EI credit is calculated based on contributions and premiums, providing a reduction in federal tax payable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be3c8254ac3b81df856eab05e2babc4e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101151</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tax Credits">
      <data key="d0">Tax Credits</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax credits reduce the amount of tax payable and can be generated by CPP and EI contributions.&lt;SEP&gt;Tax credits, including BPA, CPP, and EI, reduce the amount of tax payable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be3c8254ac3b81df856eab05e2babc4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041dc2e0b32226e0b7c758a7359523f3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101190</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CRA T4">
      <data key="d0">CRA T4</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">CRA T4 is a Statement of Remuneration Paid issued by employers to report employment income and deductions for the tax year.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101186</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T4 Slip">
      <data key="d0">T4 Slip</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The T4 Slip is a document issued by employers to detail employment income and deductions for employees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101186</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T4 Box Reference Guide">
      <data key="d0">T4 Box Reference Guide</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The T4 Box Reference Guide provides detailed information about various T4 boxes, including descriptions and tax treatments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101186</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Employment Income">
      <data key="d0">Employment Income</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Employment Income refers to money received by employees in exchange for their work, reported on the T4 Slip.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101186</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CPP Contributions">
      <data key="d0">CPP Contributions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CPP Contributions are employee contributions to the Canada Pension Plan, reported on T4 slips for tax purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101186</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="QPP Contributions">
      <data key="d0">QPP Contributions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">QPP Contributions are contributions to the Quebec Pension Plan, specifically for Quebec residents, included in T4 reporting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101186</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="EI Premiums">
      <data key="d0">EI Premiums</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">EI Premiums are amounts deducted from an employee's salary for Employment Insurance and reported on the T4 Slip.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101186</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RPP Contributions">
      <data key="d0">RPP Contributions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">RPP Contributions are amounts employees contribute to Registered Pension Plans and can be deducted from taxable income.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101187</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Taxable Allowances">
      <data key="d0">Taxable Allowances</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Taxable Allowances are benefits provided by employers that must be reported as income on the T4 Slip.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101188</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Union Dues">
      <data key="d0">Union Dues</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Dues are fees paid by employees to their unions, which can be deducted from gross income.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101188</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Charitable Donations">
      <data key="d0">Charitable Donations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Charitable Donations are contributions made to registered charities, eligible for tax credits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f7c5cf2323ead79ef1bb328c9701238d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101188</data>
