    <node id="HBP">
      <data key="d0">HBP</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">HBP stands for Home Buyers' Plan, a tax strategy allowing first-time home purchases through an interest-free loan from personal savings.&lt;SEP&gt;HBP stands for Home Buyers' Plan, allowing withdrawals from an RRSP to buy or build a qualifying home without immediate tax consequences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534ea8e212706659d6a83a6fde877e5d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tax Planning Strategies">
      <data key="d0">Tax Planning Strategies</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax planning strategies, specifically related to RRSPs, aim to optimize tax benefits and savings for individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Tax Planning Strategies with FHSAs include various methods to maximize tax advantages and growth for first-time home buyers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534ea8e212706659d6a83a6fde877e5d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tax Bracket">
      <data key="d0">Tax Bracket</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A tax bracket refers to a range of income that is taxed at a specific rate, affecting the value of deductions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101328</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RRSP">
      <data key="d0">RRSP</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">RRSP stands for Registered Retirement Savings Plan, a tax-advantaged savings account for retirement in Canada.&lt;SEP&gt;Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) is a retirement savings plan that provides tax advantages for Canadians saving for retirement.&lt;SEP&gt;RRSP, or Registered Retirement Savings Plan, is a retirement savings plan that individuals use in Canada to defer taxes on contributions.&lt;SEP&gt;RRSP stands for Registered Retirement Savings Plan, a savings account with tax advantages for retirement purposes in Canada.&lt;SEP&gt;RRSP stands for Registered Retirement Savings Plan, allowing Canadians to save for retirement with tax-deductible contributions and tax-sheltered investment growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b52c763122110f77d0bf6ccf9c8f8507&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6da06f6e3dca271d80baa141c0aef4d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534ea8e212706659d6a83a6fde877e5d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369637</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Higher Tax Bracket">
      <data key="d0">Higher Tax Bracket</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Being in a higher tax bracket refers to a status where individuals have higher income levels and therefore pay taxes at a greater rate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101328</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Income Splitting">
      <data key="d0">Income Splitting</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Income splitting is a tax strategy that allows couples to reduce their overall tax burden by distributing income between partners.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101328</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tax-Deferred Growth">
      <data key="d0">Tax-Deferred Growth</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax-deferred growth is the increase in value of an investment that grows without being taxed until withdrawals are made.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101329</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Registered Retirement Savings Plan">
      <data key="d0">Registered Retirement Savings Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) is a tax-advantaged savings plan registered with the Canada Revenue Agency, allowing for tax-deductible contributions and tax-deferred investment growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101329</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canada Revenue Agency">
      <data key="d0">Canada Revenue Agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Revenue Agency (CRA) is the governmental body responsible for tax collection and administration in Canada, overseeing Registered Retirement Savings Plans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d66ea5179b3a914a2b6215ce0d8004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101329</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RRSP Deduction Limit">
      <data key="d0">RRSP Deduction Limit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The RRSP deduction limit defines the maximum amount an individual can deduct for RRSP contributions in a tax year.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101330</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
