    </node>
    <node id="BC">
      <data key="d0">BC</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">BC is a Canadian province that still offers provincial tuition credits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-763b1c1e1aaf51a4f6b35169530a488f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369230</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alberta">
      <data key="d0">Alberta</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Alberta is a Canadian province that still offers provincial tuition credits.&lt;SEP&gt;Alberta is a Canadian province that announced tax bracket indexation.&lt;SEP&gt;Alberta is a province known for the lowest tax rate, making it favorable for high earners.&lt;SEP&gt;Alberta is a Canadian province that provides a range of tax credits and benefits for individuals and families.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-763b1c1e1aaf51a4f6b35169530a488f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03bb900cab8fd043392cad33c9c60640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-613f1fae239716a1ed056696bcae297d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6767fe1983997e5594e2d1e81f3962</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772370161</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Provincial Tuition Tax Credit">
      <data key="d0">Provincial Tuition Tax Credit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Provincial tuition tax credits are specific to provinces and may vary, with some provinces eliminating or maintaining the credits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-763b1c1e1aaf51a4f6b35169530a488f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369230</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Professional Examination Fees">
      <data key="d0">Professional Examination Fees</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Professional examination fees include fees for certifications like CPA, bar admission, and medical licensing, and are eligible for tax credits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-763b1c1e1aaf51a4f6b35169530a488f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369231</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carryforward">
      <data key="d0">Carryforward</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-763b1c1e1aaf51a4f6b35169530a488f</data>
      <data key="d2">Schedule 11 is used to track carryforward tuition amounts on the T1 return.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369236</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T1 Individual Tax Return">
      <data key="d0">T1 Individual Tax Return</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The T1 Individual Tax Return is a form used by individuals in Canada to file their personal taxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369296</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Revenu Québec">
      <data key="d0">Revenu Québec</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Revenu Québec is the provincial revenue agency that manages tax collection and returns in Quebec.&lt;SEP&gt;Revenu Québec is the provincial tax administration in Quebec responsible for collecting taxes and administering the tax system in the province.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-936dddac80917fe456d3727287e9f980</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772370218</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="FHSA">
      <data key="d0">FHSA</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">FHSA refers to a type of savings account whose contributions are deductible on the tax return within the specified calendar year.&lt;SEP&gt;FHSA stands for First Home Savings Account, a tax-advantaged savings account for home purchase purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-534ea8e212706659d6a83a6fde877e5d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canada Carbon Rebate">
      <data key="d0">Canada Carbon Rebate</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Carbon Rebate is a benefit aligned with the GST/HST credit, paid to individuals to offset carbon tax costs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Canada Carbon Rebate, formerly known as the Climate Action Incentive Payment, is a quarterly payment to offset federal carbon pricing for residents in specific provinces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Canada Carbon Rebate is a program that allows Alberta residents to receive a rebate by filing annually.&lt;SEP&gt;The Canada Carbon Rebate offers financial rebates to residents affected by carbon pricing policies, providing quarterly payments based on various criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;The Canada Carbon Rebate program provides financial rebates to residents of various provinces in Canada based on carbon-related costs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Canada Carbon Rebate program facilitates financial support to individuals based on their carbon emissions impact.&lt;SEP&gt;The Canada Carbon Rebate program in Manitoba provides quarterly payments to eligible residents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d66ea5179b3a914a2b6215ce0d8004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dd1ab2e92259b216c4f87314232a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-613f1fae239716a1ed056696bcae297d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6767fe1983997e5594e2d1e81f3962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11c553d9c05dddfa3309447cb2baa12c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-641c0fe12d176236fe97fad76cedd6ee</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772370270</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Quebec Solidarity Credit">
      <data key="d0">Quebec Solidarity Credit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Quebec Solidarity Credit is a monthly payment to Quebec residents, aimed at reducing the tax burden.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quebec Solidarity Credit is a financial benefit for residents based on family size and income level.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quebec Solidarity Credit is a financial assistance program aimed at low-income residents, offering substantial benefits to eligible taxpayers.&lt;SEP&gt;Quebec Solidarity Credit is a financial benefit that combines several components to assist low-income residents, based on family income.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e6767fe1983997e5594e2d1e81f3962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-936dddac80917fe456d3727287e9f980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d33a716738be034afb001ad0bfbefeb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772370219</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Instalment Payments">
      <data key="d0">Instalment Payments</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Instalment payments are quarterly tax payments required for individuals owing more than certain thresholds in net tax.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369299</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T4 Slips">
      <data key="d0">T4 Slips</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">T4 slips are statements employers issue to employees, detailing income and deductions within the tax year.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369299</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T5 Slips">
      <data key="d0">T5 Slips</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">T5 slips are statements for investment income, issued by financial institutions to investors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369299</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Notice of Objection">
      <data key="d0">Notice of Objection</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">A Notice of Objection is filed by a taxpayer to dispute an assessment or reassessment made by the CRA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369299</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CRA Reassessment Period">
      <data key="d0">CRA Reassessment Period</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The CRA Reassessment Period is the time frame during which the CRA can reassess a tax return, generally three years from the original assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369300</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Request for Adjustment (T1-ADJ)">
      <data key="d0">Request for Adjustment (T1-ADJ)</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">The Request for Adjustment is a form that allows taxpayers to request changes to their tax returns for up to ten previous years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369300</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RRSP Conversion">
      <data key="d0">RRSP Conversion</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">RRSP conversion refers to the process of changing an RRSP into a RRIF or annuity by the end of the year that an account holder turns 71.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369301</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Home Buyers' Plan (HBP)">
      <data key="d0">Home Buyers' Plan (HBP)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Home Buyers' Plan allows first-time home buyers to withdraw RRSP funds without tax penalty, requiring repayments over 15 years.&lt;SEP&gt;The Home Buyers' Plan (HBP) allows Canadians to withdraw from their RRSPs to buy a first home, requiring repayment over 15 years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6da06f6e3dca271d80baa141c0aef4d6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lifelong Learning Plan (LLP)">
      <data key="d0">Lifelong Learning Plan (LLP)</data>
      <data key="d1">program</data>
      <data key="d2">The Lifelong Learning Plan allows students to withdraw RRSP funds for educational purposes, requiring repayments over 10 years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369301</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Notice of Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Notice of Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Notice of Assessment is a document issued by the CRA detailing the determination of tax liabilities or refunds after a tax return is processed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369301</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Notice of Reassessment">
      <data key="d0">Notice of Reassessment</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Notice of Reassessment is a document issued by the CRA indicating changes to a previously assessed tax return, often due to additional information or corrections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369301</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Quebec TP-1">
      <data key="d0">Quebec TP-1</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Quebec TP-1 is a tax return form that Quebec residents must file with Revenu Québec to report their income and taxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369301</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="First 60 Days RRSP Contribution Period">
      <data key="d0">First 60 Days RRSP Contribution Period</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The First 60 Days RRSP Contribution Period allows contributions made during the first 60 days of a new year to be applied to the prior year’s tax return or the current year’s.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61aebf2ad198d778d2af95f014d9c782</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369302</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Employed Filing Deadline">
      <data key="d0">Self-Employed Filing Deadline</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">The self-employed filing deadline for tax reporting falls on June 15, 2025, but will be on June 16, 2025, since June 15 is a Sunday.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc0b482656c1fbfddee8368d8616fa29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369302</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Last Day for 2025 TFSA and FHSA Contributions">
      <data key="d0">Last Day for 2025 TFSA and FHSA Contributions</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">December 31, 2025, is the last day to make TFSA and FHSA contributions for the 2025 tax year and claim charitable donations on the 2025 return.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc0b482656c1fbfddee8368d8616fa29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369302</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Penalty for Late Filing">
      <data key="d0">Penalty for Late Filing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The penalty for late filing is calculated as 5% of the balance owing, plus 1% per full month late, up to a maximum of 17%.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc0b482656c1fbfddee8368d8616fa29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369303</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Repeat Offenders Penalty">
      <data key="d0">Repeat Offenders Penalty</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">For repeat offenders, the penalty is 10% of the balance owing, plus 2% per month late, up to a maximum of 50%.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc0b482656c1fbfddee8368d8616fa29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369303</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Interest on Unpaid Tax">
      <data key="d0">Interest on Unpaid Tax</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Revenue Agency charges compound daily interest on unpaid tax balances, with rates changing quarterly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc0b482656c1fbfddee8368d8616fa29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369303</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prescribed Interest Rate">
      <data key="d0">Prescribed Interest Rate</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The prescribed interest rate by the CRA for Q1 2025 is 8% for overdue taxes and 4% for refunds.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc0b482656c1fbfddee8368d8616fa29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369303</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Balance Owing">
      <data key="d0">Balance Owing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Balance owing refers to the amount due on taxes, impacting the calculation of late filing penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc0b482656c1fbfddee8368d8616fa29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369303</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Benefit Payments">
      <data key="d0">Benefit Payments</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Benefit payments are entitlements that require tax filing to be received despite no penalties if no taxes are owed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc0b482656c1fbfddee8368d8616fa29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369304</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Q1 2025">
      <data key="d0">Q1 2025</data>
      <data key="d1">timeperiod</data>
      <data key="d2">Q1 2025 refers to the first quarter of the year 2025, during which specific interest rates for overdue taxes and refunds apply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc0b482656c1fbfddee8368d8616fa29</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369304</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="April 30, 2025">
