      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369308</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Registered Retirement Income Fund (RRIF)">
      <data key="d0">Registered Retirement Income Fund (RRIF)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Registered Retirement Income Fund is a retirement income vehicle where withdrawals count as income for GIS purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369349</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Disability Tax Credit (DTC)">
      <data key="d0">Disability Tax Credit (DTC)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Disability Tax Credit is a federal non-refundable tax credit available for individuals with severe and prolonged impairments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369349</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Registered Disability Savings Plan (RDSP)">
      <data key="d0">Registered Disability Savings Plan (RDSP)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Registered Disability Savings Plan is a long-term savings plan for individuals eligible for the Disability Tax Credit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369349</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canada Disability Savings Grant (CDSG)">
      <data key="d0">Canada Disability Savings Grant (CDSG)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Disability Savings Grant is a government matching contribution to RDSPs, up to $3,500 per year and $70,000 lifetime.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369349</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canada Disability Savings Bond (CDSB)">
      <data key="d0">Canada Disability Savings Bond (CDSB)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Disability Savings Bond is a government contribution to RDSPs for low-income individuals, up to $1,000 per year and $20,000 lifetime.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369351</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Expense Tax Credit (METC)">
      <data key="d0">Medical Expense Tax Credit (METC)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Medical Expense Tax Credit is a non-refundable credit for medical expenses exceeding a specified threshold.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369351</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Refundable Medical Expense Supplement">
      <data key="d0">Refundable Medical Expense Supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Refundable Medical Expense Supplement is an additional refundable credit for low-income working individuals based on METC claimed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369351</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canada Pension Plan (CPP) Benefits">
      <data key="d0">Canada Pension Plan (CPP) Benefits</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Canada Pension Plan Benefits include retirement pensions based on contributions, with options for early, standard, and deferred benefits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369352</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Employment Insurance (EI) Benefits">
      <data key="d0">Employment Insurance (EI) Benefits</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Employment Insurance Benefits provide temporary financial support, including regular, maternity, and parental benefits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369352</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canada Workers Benefit (CWB) Disability Supplement">
      <data key="d0">Canada Workers Benefit (CWB) Disability Supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Workers Benefit Disability Supplement provides additional support for individuals with disabilities who are eligible for the Disability Tax Credit and are part of the workforce.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369352</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Child Disability Benefit">
      <data key="d0">Child Disability Benefit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Child Disability Benefit is a program providing financial assistance to families caring for children with disabilities and requires DTC eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369353</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Form T2201">
      <data key="d0">Form T2201</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Form T2201 is the form used to apply for the Disability Tax Credit, needing certification by a medical practitioner.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369353</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="2024 CPP Maximum Increase">
      <data key="d0">2024 CPP Maximum Increase</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">The maximum increase in CPP retirement pension for deferral from age 65 to 70 is 42%.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9b8c864baf455d682e0b304e5f7a954e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369353</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canada Workers Benefit">
      <data key="d0">Canada Workers Benefit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Workers Benefit is a refundable credit for low-income working individuals and families, replacing the former Working Income Tax Benefit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21d66ea5179b3a914a2b6215ce0d8004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369354</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Old Age Security">
      <data key="d0">Old Age Security</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Old Age Security is a monthly payment to Canadians aged 65 and older, based on years of residency, with provisions for income-related clawbacks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21d66ea5179b3a914a2b6215ce0d8004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369354</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Guaranteed Income Supplement">
      <data key="d0">Guaranteed Income Supplement</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Guaranteed Income Supplement is a monthly payment for low-income OAS recipients, fully income-tested with reductions based on non-OAS income.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21d66ea5179b3a914a2b6215ce0d8004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369355</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Disability Tax Credit">
      <data key="d0">Disability Tax Credit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Disability Tax Credit is a non-refundable federal credit for individuals with severe and prolonged impairments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Disability Tax Credit has expanded eligibility criteria for individuals with mental health conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21d66ea5179b3a914a2b6215ce0d8004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03bb900cab8fd043392cad33c9c60640</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369781</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Federal Carbon Pricing">
      <data key="d0">Federal Carbon Pricing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Federal Carbon Pricing refers to the pricing structure set by the federal government for carbon emissions, affecting rebates like the Canada Carbon Rebate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21d66ea5179b3a914a2b6215ce0d8004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369355</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CRA Publications">
      <data key="d0">CRA Publications</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">CRA Publications are official documents published by the Canada Revenue Agency, providing guidance on tax and benefit programs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21d66ea5179b3a914a2b6215ce0d8004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369355</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Income Threshold">
      <data key="d0">Income Threshold</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Income Threshold is a financial limit used to determine the reduction or eligibility for various benefits, such as the GST/HST Credit and Canada Child Benefit.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21d66ea5179b3a914a2b6215ce0d8004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772369355</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
